## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-account trust, least privilege S3/KMS usage, no Internet constraint, and auditability.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account role trust
- S3 bucket policy with path-level scoping
- KMS policy for decrypt/encrypt
- No Internet access
- Immutable auditing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy excerpt for DataAccessRole
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A:role/ProcessorRole"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```
```javascript
// Bucket policy excerpt (data-inbound)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B:role/DataAccessRole"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-inbound",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-inbound/data-inbound/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B:role/DataAccessRole"},
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-out/*"
    }
  ]
}
```
```javascript
// KMS key policy snippet (CMK in Security account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B:role/DataAccessRole"},
      "Action": ["kms:Decrypt","kms:GenerateDataKey*","kms:Encrypt"],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for privilege creep?
- How would you rotate the CMK without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical mastery of tenant isolation, cross-account access, and automated containment in AWS, plus how to validate security controls under real-world pressures.

## Key Concepts

- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag for tenant-scoped access
- S3 Access Points and per-tenant prefixes for isolation
- Tenant-scoped KMS keys with rotation
- EventBridge + Lambda + Step Functions for rapid containment
- Immutable audit trails with CloudTrail and S3 Object Lock

## Code Example

```javascript
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket","s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What signals would trigger the containment workflow and how would you test them?
- How would you validate that rotation and ABAC policies cannot be bypassed during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a secure, cross-account multi-tenant streaming architecture with strict tenant isolation, fine-grained access controls, key management best practices, and rapid incident response capabilities in a production data pipeline context.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account trust relationships with ABAC and MFA enforcement
- Tenant isolation across streaming data paths using account boundaries
- Per-tenant KMS keys with automatic rotation for cryptographic isolation
- PrivateLink/VPC endpoints for private, encrypted data transit without internet exposure
- Immutable audit trails using CloudTrail, S3 Object Lock, and Lake Formation access controls
- Automated breach containment workflow with sub-minute response times

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": ["kinesis:PutRecord", "kinesis:PutRecords"],
    "Resource": "arn:aws:kinesis:*:*:stream/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}/*",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {
        "aws:SourceAccount": "${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}",
        "aws:RequestedRegion": ["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]
      },
      "ArnEquals": {
        "aws:SourceArn": "arn:aws:kinesis:*:*:stream/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}/*"
      },
      "Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"}
    }
  }]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical tenant isolation pattern in a single AWS account using core services, focusing on real-world constraints for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation with DynamoDB LeadingKeys and per-tenant partition keys
- IAM policy conditions using ForAllValues:StringEquals and PrincipalTag
- API Gateway/Lambda authorizer to inject TenantId into requests
- Auditing and testability with CloudTrail data events

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:GetItem","dynamodb:PutItem","dynamodb:Query"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:region:acct:table/TenantTable",
      "Condition": {
        "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
          "dynamodb:LeadingKeys": ["TENANT#${aws:PrincipalTag/TenantId}"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without downtime?
- How would you test breach scenarios with cross-tenant access attempts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests tenant isolation, cross‑account access, and rapid containment in a simple, reproducible pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑account IAM roles with restricted trust
- S3 per‑tenant prefixes and least privilege in bucket policies
- Server‑side encryption (SSE‑KMS) and key rotation
- Immutable auditability and rapid containment of breaches

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example trust policy snippet (Account B role trusting Account A data role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A:role/DataReaderForTenant*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "tenant-<id>-read"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```javascript
// Example bucket policy restricting to tenant prefix
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B:role/AnalyticsRead"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data-bucket/tenant-<id>/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate keys per tenant and handle revocation?
- How would you automate breach simulations and containment checks?
